From 31b1b1a9cfd88c83086f72fee0630fb7b750712e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccicnce113424 <ccicnce113424@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:06:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nixos/dbus: register D-Bus service packages in
 services.dbus.packages

#549241 stops the D-Bus daemons from searching the system profile, so a
package's D-Bus configuration only reaches them once a module lists it in
services.dbus.packages.

The packages were selected mechanically: nix-index was queried for every
package carrying dbus-1 configuration, hits whose paths are only empty
directories or symlinks were dropped, and the remaining names were matched
against nixos/modules both as pkgs.NAME references and as mkPackageOption
defaults, which text search alone misses.  The result was then checked by
evaluation: for 45 NixOS configurations, environment.systemPackages was
compared against services.dbus.packages and every unregistered package
reported.  Only systemd stays out, since #549241 registers it itself.

A registration mirrors the statement that installs the package, its conditions
and its excludePackages filter included, so environment.plasma6.excludePackages
drops a package from both sides.  Packages that only reach systemd.packages,
services.udev.packages or the X11/Wayland session path stay out, as do those
only reachable through xdg.portal.extraPortals, which config/xdg/portal.nix
covers.

Merge together with (or after) #549241: on master alone system.path is still a
D-Bus search path, so each registered package is found twice.

Assisted-by: omp:Space Bunny Alpha
